## The three fixes

F53 (X-P8-14): `storytimeCardMatchSource` in `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/card-kit.ts` read the third column of a match line with `fields[2] ?? ''` and returned `none` only when that column was the empty string. A third column of white space held no row id, so the function returned `picture` and the count of the build over-counted the pictures. The fix returns `none` when the third column is empty after a trim. `storytimeCardMatchCounts` uses that function, so it counts such a line as `none`. The JSDoc of the function names the rule.

F54 (X-P8-15): `storytimeCardPictureMatchLines` wrote the label of a card into column 2 as it stands, so a label with a tab or a line break gave a line of five columns or more lines than cards. The fix writes the label through the new function `matchLabel`, which replaces each run of white space and of the control characters (C0, DEL, C1) with one space. The label keeps its padding, so a card of a padded label still names no row. The shipped labels hold no such character, so the shipped match report stays byte for byte the same.

F55 (X-P8-16): `STICKER_CENTRE_PATTERN` used `\s`, which accepts a separator that CSS does not accept. Chrome ignores `object-position:20%<no-break space>80%` and prints the sticker at the default centre, so the override did nothing without an error. The fix uses `[ \t\n\f\r]+`, the white space of CSS. The values of `STORYTIME_STICKER_CENTER_OVERRIDES`, the sticker layout, the patch colors, and the dot counts stay the same.

The three `it.fails` markers of X-P8-14 (line 41), X-P8-15 (line 81), and X-P8-16 (line 142) in `dashboard/__tests__/storytime-print-card-kit-adversarial-r3.test.ts` are now `it`. The precedent is commit 03e20aac and commit 9ef650dd. No other line of any test file changed.

